# 9. EDITABLE MOVEMENT PATHS AND CURVES

I want to control movement paths visually.

I do not want every character movement to be restricted to a straight line.

For example, when a character jumps, I want to create an arc.

When a character walks across a scene, I want to control the route.

Build a simple editable motion-path system.

## 9.1 Motion path editor

Allow me to:

- Create movement points.
- Select points.
- Move points.
- Add points.
- Delete points.
- Adjust handles.
- Change curve smoothness.
- Preview the path.

Use Bezier curves or another appropriate spline representation.

## 9.2 Visual editing

Display the path in the viewport when a character is selected and its motion path is enabled.

The path should be subtle and visible enough to edit.

I should be able to adjust handles similarly to editing curves in a vector design application.

## 9.3 Motion evaluation

The character must follow the actual edited curve during playback.

Do not merely draw a curve that has no effect on movement.

The motion-path system should work with timeline duration and character animation.

Support a simple option for movement direction/orientation along the path if feasible.

