# 17. PERFORMANCE AND ENGINE QUALITY

The studio must remain usable with multiple characters and audio tracks.

Avoid unnecessary rerenders.

Avoid recreating the 3D renderer on every UI update.

Keep the rendering engine separate from the interface.

Use efficient update loops.

Dispose of unused:

- Geometry.
- Materials.
- Textures.
- Audio buffers.
- Render targets.
- Event listeners.
- Animation resources.

Prevent memory leaks when changing scenes or removing characters.

Use a consistent animation clock.

Do not let multiple competing requestAnimationFrame loops control the same engine.

Avoid running duplicate audio playback instances.

